document: README.md
blob: 1d0e9a079f37bf50e84f55e087c2a05e873aabec
decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Developers and reviewers who use the standard
purpose: How to attach the standard to a project and what each command and gate checks

README.md is now the English default README for developers and reviewers who use the standard, with a
language switcher to README.ko.md (GitHub convention: README.md + README.<lang>.md).
Translated every section of the previous Korean README without dropping commands, flags, ADR links,
limits or conditions: setup's eight steps, teammate prerequisites, failure handling, Windows/LF notes,
locked-revision execution, adoption, check scope, OS-specific commands, commit/MR gate, branch model,
tracker contract, document types and editorial review.
Added two subheadings (Attaching to Claude Code, Branch model) to split long sections; content unchanged.
Kept Korean where it is real output or contract value: setup's failure output block (the CLI prints
Korean), the example commit/PR titles, the label example `결함`, and MR section `영향 및 후속 작업` /
`없음` with English glosses.
Limitation: setup's Korean CLI output is shown as-is; the CLI itself was not localized in this change.

